WEBVTT

1
00:01:48,576 --> 00:01:50,210
-Come on...

2
00:02:03,057 --> 00:02:04,491
Come on...

3
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:27,582
One day, a man went
to take a walk into town.

4
00:02:27,682 --> 00:02:32,654
On his way home he saw a little
dog which had hurt his leg

5
00:02:33,755 --> 00:02:35,123
The poor dog was so lame

6
00:02:35,222 --> 00:02:37,224
he could not lift his foot off

7
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:39,493
the ground without great pain.

8
00:03:02,917 --> 00:03:04,519
-Aren't you gonna eat, Lucas?

9
00:03:04,619 --> 00:03:07,354
<i>- </i> I'll have mine later, Jacob.

10
00:03:59,941 --> 00:04:02,409
-Lucas, look!

11
00:05:10,912 --> 00:05:12,613
<i>- </i> Get your ass over here!

12
00:05:28,196 --> 00:05:31,933
-Sorriest God damn hogs
I've ever seen, Christ almighty.

13
00:05:32,033 --> 00:05:35,368
2 and 25 per..
4 and 50 for the both of 'em

14
00:05:35,468 --> 00:05:36,304
it's the best I can do.

15
00:05:36,403 --> 00:05:38,239
-In October you
was giving 5 per.

16
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:39,307
-It ain't October no more.

17
00:05:39,406 --> 00:05:43,343
Christ, this Gilt's as scrawny
as you are.

18
00:05:43,678 --> 00:05:46,514
-What about one of the horses?

19
00:06:04,532 --> 00:06:05,498
-4 and 50 for the hogs...

20
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:09,136
25 for the swayback in addition.
Deal?

21
00:06:12,907 --> 00:06:14,542
<i>- </i> I'll take that
cornmeal right there

22
00:06:14,642 --> 00:06:16,476
<i>and the rye flour...</i>

23
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:19,680
Some beans and that hard bread.

24
00:06:19,981 --> 00:06:22,415
-Okay... let's see...

25
00:06:22,516 --> 00:06:27,454
That's a quarter dollar
for the bread times two.

26
00:06:27,555 --> 00:06:29,657
Even dollar for the beans

27
00:06:29,757 --> 00:06:34,695
and 3 and 50 for the meal
and the flour.

28
00:06:35,863 --> 00:06:39,367
Say uh, Tom Langtry come by...

29
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:42,603
Tom the older,
not his boy up in Stafford.

30
00:06:42,703 --> 00:06:47,041
Remarked that he might be in the
market for some land nearabout.

31
00:06:47,141 --> 00:06:48,408
-No, thanks, Mr. Cochrane.

32
00:06:48,509 --> 00:06:49,543
- You sure, Lucas?
<i>- We're fine, sir.</i>

33
00:06:49,644 --> 00:06:50,745
<i>- </i> It could be a lot of money--

34
00:06:50,845 --> 00:06:53,014
<i>-</i> I'm gonna need another pound
of that salt beef...

35
00:06:53,114 --> 00:06:56,483
A couple cans of molasses and
three sacks of that Indian corn.

36
00:06:56,584 --> 00:06:59,553
-All right, well that's 20 cents
on the beef...

37
00:06:59,654 --> 00:07:00,888
I keep the corn down
in the cellar

38
00:07:00,988 --> 00:07:02,256
if you wanna bring
your wagon around

39
00:07:02,356 --> 00:07:04,025
I'll go down
and get it for you.

40
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:04,892
-Okay.

41
00:07:05,059 --> 00:07:07,795
-Say uh... you think
the little one could

42
00:07:07,895 --> 00:07:10,463
help his self to a candy stick?

43
00:07:10,564 --> 00:07:12,600
Red Bird peppermint, I believe.

44
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:16,637
-Okay. But you can't have it til
after supper, okay?

45
00:07:22,209 --> 00:07:23,878
Jacob!

46
00:07:24,078 --> 00:07:27,181
<i>Heard his mama wasn't nothing</i>
but a dried up old whore...

47
00:07:27,281 --> 00:07:31,619
- <i>Killed herself</i>
<i>all crazy from syphilis.</i>

48
00:07:32,286 --> 00:07:33,054
<i>Shit!</i>

49
00:07:33,421 --> 00:07:35,990
<i>That little son of a bitch</i>
just bit me!

50
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:38,125
<i>I said hold him, damnit!</i>

51
00:07:44,031 --> 00:07:45,700
You little bastard!

52
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,268
<i>- </i> All right that's enough!

53
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,672
<i>- </i> That's enough!

54
00:07:51,772 --> 00:07:53,174
<i>What have you done here?</i>

55
00:07:53,274 --> 00:07:54,375
<i>What did you do to my boy?!</i>

56
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:55,443
-That's enough, I said!

57
00:07:55,543 --> 00:07:56,610
-Like hell it is!

58
00:07:56,811 --> 00:07:58,713
That little grubstake
damn dear brained my son!

59
00:07:58,813 --> 00:08:01,515
-We didn't do nothing to him pa,
he just come at us--

60
00:08:01,615 --> 00:08:03,117
-You shut your coward mouth!

61
00:08:03,217 --> 00:08:04,251
-Charles!

62
00:08:05,019 --> 00:08:08,389
You will not be beating this
or any other child in my store,

63
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:09,457
do you understand me?

64
00:08:09,557 --> 00:08:12,226
-Just let go... let go of me.

65
00:08:14,228 --> 00:08:15,529
-Lucas...

66
00:08:15,629 --> 00:08:16,496
You better get on home now.

67
00:08:16,797 --> 00:08:19,700
Go on, get your brother and go,
both of you.

68
00:08:22,036 --> 00:08:23,838
Go!

69
00:08:23,938 --> 00:08:25,272
Hey.

70
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:28,142
Get your boys.

71
00:08:29,944 --> 00:08:32,680
-They took my peppermint stick.

72
00:08:50,431 --> 00:08:52,133
- <i>Lucas?</i>

73
00:08:52,233 --> 00:08:54,735
<i>Someone's coming.</i>

74
00:09:00,274 --> 00:09:02,576
-Stay put, you hear me?

75
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:08,449
-That old Springfield's as
liable to blow up in your hands

76
00:09:08,549 --> 00:09:10,251
as it is to fire off a shot.

77
00:09:10,351 --> 00:09:11,485
-You ain't got business here.

78
00:09:11,619 --> 00:09:12,453
-The hell I don't.

79
00:09:13,087 --> 00:09:16,791
You laid that hickory to my boy,
you took on a debt.

80
00:09:16,891 --> 00:09:18,092
I come to see it satisfied.

81
00:09:18,192 --> 00:09:20,494
They was beating on my brother.

82
00:09:20,594 --> 00:09:22,930
-One arm,
I'll get down off this horse

83
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:26,233
-and I'll whoop your ass--
-You keep quiet!

84
00:09:28,537 --> 00:09:30,037
-I ain't going with you.

85
00:09:30,137 --> 00:09:31,105
-The hell you ain't.

86
00:09:31,205 --> 00:09:33,874
I got two hundred beeves
on contract...

87
00:09:33,974 --> 00:09:36,110
You're gonna have to work off
what his broke arm

88
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:39,847
can't if'n I gotta drag you
outta here.

89
00:09:40,614 --> 00:09:42,183
This is a hard land, son.

90
00:09:42,283 --> 00:09:44,752
You might be
between the hay and the grass

91
00:09:44,852 --> 00:09:48,189
but that don't make it
no less the case.

92
00:09:48,489 --> 00:09:52,293
I'll come back 'round
to collect you in the morning.

93
00:10:06,474 --> 00:10:08,342
-Get to sleep now.

94
00:10:11,479 --> 00:10:13,347
-Lucas?

95
00:10:14,181 --> 00:10:16,784
What did Mama look like?

96
00:10:21,722 --> 00:10:23,991
-I can't remember.

97
00:12:28,382 --> 00:12:29,651
-Lucas Hollister...

98
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:30,751
As you have been found guilty

99
00:12:30,851 --> 00:12:33,287
of the murder
of Charles Edward Gantry

100
00:12:33,387 --> 00:12:36,924
by a jury in good standing
in Sedgwick County

101
00:12:37,024 --> 00:12:41,630
on this day, 4th April,
18 and 82.

102
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:46,934
And though taking into account,
your youth and circumstances

103
00:12:47,034 --> 00:12:50,871
by virtue of your prior history
with the deceased,

104
00:12:50,971 --> 00:12:53,675
this court has no recourse

105
00:12:53,774 --> 00:12:57,978
but to find this heinous act
premeditated.

106
00:12:58,078 --> 00:13:04,184
As such, Lucas Hollister,
I hereby sentence you to hang...

107
00:13:04,285 --> 00:13:08,922
Sentence to be carried out upon
construction of a suitable venue

108
00:13:09,023 --> 00:13:12,426
and disptach of the Hangman
from Lincoln.

109
00:13:12,527 --> 00:13:14,128
This court is adjourned.

110
00:13:34,882 --> 00:13:36,551
- <i>I can appreciate</i>
<i>that you've come</i>

111
00:13:36,651 --> 00:13:38,018
<i>quite a distance,</i>
Ms. Bassett,

112
00:13:38,118 --> 00:13:39,286
<i>but we can't just--</i>

113
00:13:39,453 --> 00:13:41,723
- <i>Do not speak to me</i>
<i>as if we are acquainted,</i>

114
00:13:41,822 --> 00:13:43,023
<i>Mr. Tyrell.</i>

115
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:44,458
- <i>I do apologize,</i>
<i>Ms. Bassett, but again--</i>

116
00:13:44,559 --> 00:13:47,294
-The distance I have traveled is
of no consequence

117
00:13:47,394 --> 00:13:48,095
to this discussion.

118
00:13:48,429 --> 00:13:49,863
- <i>The boy's</i>
<i>been tried, Ms. Bassett,</i>

119
00:13:50,064 --> 00:13:51,700
<i>-he's been convicted--</i>
<i>-In Hayesville.</i>

120
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,767
<i>Yes but--</i>

121
00:13:52,866 --> 00:13:53,967
-A saltlick backwater
to say the least.

122
00:13:54,101 --> 00:13:56,337
- <i>Please try</i>
and understand, Ms. Bassett--

123
00:13:56,437 --> 00:13:59,306
-I will hire a lawyer.
I'll appeal to the state court.

124
00:13:59,406 --> 00:14:02,009
- <i>I am a judge of the</i>
state court, Ms. Bassett...

125
00:14:02,109 --> 00:14:05,846
<i>Duly appointed by</i>
Territorial Governor John Geary

126
00:14:05,946 --> 00:14:08,015
<i>in 18 and 54.</i>

127
00:14:08,115 --> 00:14:11,553
<i>27 years on in Sedgwick.</i>

128
00:14:11,653 --> 00:14:13,187
<i>And while I esteem your call</i>

129
00:14:13,287 --> 00:14:17,324
<i>-to plead the boy's--</i>
-To hell with your esteem.

130
00:14:17,424 --> 00:14:19,360
Psalm 82:3...

131
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:24,465
Give justice to the weak
and to the fatherless.

132
00:14:38,412 --> 00:14:40,180
Do you know me?

133
00:14:41,482 --> 00:14:43,450
-No, Ma'am.

134
00:14:43,551 --> 00:14:46,420
-Look at me when you speak.

135
00:14:46,521 --> 00:14:49,123
Barely a sprout you are.

136
00:14:49,223 --> 00:14:51,826
They tell me I'm kin to you.

137
00:14:51,925 --> 00:14:55,396
Your mother
was Wilhelmina Hollister?

138
00:14:56,564 --> 00:14:58,499
My name is Evelyn Bassett.

139
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:01,268
Bassetts of Sheridan County.

140
00:15:02,169 --> 00:15:04,338
I was Aunt to your mother.

141
00:15:04,438 --> 00:15:08,743
Though it's been some years
since we had occasion.

142
00:15:08,843 --> 00:15:12,246
I thought it only proper
to come.

143
00:15:12,913 --> 00:15:14,181
-Can you help me?

144
00:15:14,281 --> 00:15:19,186
-It appears my entreaties
have fallen upon deaf ears.

145
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:22,456
-What'll happen to my brother?

146
00:15:22,557 --> 00:15:26,260
-Arrangements will have
to be made.

147
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,762
-A boy's home?

148
00:15:27,862 --> 00:15:30,497
-I expect.

149
00:15:30,598 --> 00:15:32,534
-Can you take him?

150
00:15:32,634 --> 00:15:34,001
-Certainly not.

151
00:15:34,101 --> 00:15:37,137
-He won't have no one
once I'm gone.

152
00:15:37,237 --> 00:15:40,140
-I'm an old woman, Lucas.

153
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:43,878
This is simply
the way of things.

154
00:15:43,977 --> 00:15:46,480
-Why'd you come then?

155
00:15:46,581 --> 00:15:49,149
-To see for myself.

156
00:15:53,621 --> 00:16:01,161
Your mother was very dear to me
when she was a child.

157
00:16:03,263 --> 00:16:06,066
I'm afraid I have to take
my leave of you.

158
00:16:06,166 --> 00:16:09,269
I'm sorry
I couldn't have done more.

159
00:18:08,155 --> 00:18:10,024
-Shhhh...

160
00:18:10,123 --> 00:18:12,961
My little Angel...

161
00:18:13,061 --> 00:18:14,862
I know...

162
00:18:16,064 --> 00:18:17,966
Mommy knows.

163
00:18:18,066 --> 00:18:21,301
My little Angel.

164
00:18:21,401 --> 00:18:23,938
It's okay, my darling.

165
00:18:24,606 --> 00:18:29,711
Dear Lord,
please take mercy on this child.

166
00:18:34,448 --> 00:18:37,417
You hate him for it, don't you?

167
00:18:39,219 --> 00:18:41,288
-What?

168
00:18:41,789 --> 00:18:43,891
-For dying.

169
00:18:45,693 --> 00:18:48,328
For making you hurt.

170
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,834
-Don't say that in front of him.

171
00:18:54,102 --> 00:18:58,338
-You think you can fix anything,
Wood...

172
00:18:58,438 --> 00:19:01,408
But you can't fix this.

173
00:19:10,417 --> 00:19:13,487
Why can't you look at him?

174
00:19:16,423 --> 00:19:19,493
Why can't you look at me?

175
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:41,649
-I wanna bring these sons
of bitches in clean, Drum.

176
00:19:41,749 --> 00:19:42,416
-Don't bother me none.

177
00:19:42,517 --> 00:19:44,251
Should we bring Pete along?

178
00:19:44,351 --> 00:19:46,353
-Why wake the Sheriff?

179
00:19:49,891 --> 00:19:52,093
-They's up there a piece
outside the hotel.

180
00:19:52,192 --> 00:19:54,028
Looks to be four or five of 'em.

181
00:19:54,128 --> 00:19:55,563
Charlie Blake, Frank Leslie...

182
00:19:55,663 --> 00:19:57,965
Rest of 'em's Mexicans
and Half Breeds.

183
00:19:58,066 --> 00:19:59,199
-Anybody put eyes to the girl?

184
00:19:59,299 --> 00:20:01,569
<i>Not that I seen, Marshall.</i>

185
00:20:02,837 --> 00:20:05,472
- <i>Y'all come for piece</i>
of Charlie Blake?

186
00:20:05,573 --> 00:20:07,274
<i>God damn Bullwhackers...</i>

187
00:20:07,374 --> 00:20:08,543
-They been at it all night
in there...

188
00:20:08,643 --> 00:20:11,546
Liquor
and every other damn thing.

189
00:20:11,779 --> 00:20:13,280
-Drum, you got the left,

190
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:15,016
Tom, stay right of me.

191
00:20:15,116 --> 00:20:15,883
Keep your head.

192
00:20:15,983 --> 00:20:19,520
If anything happens, get low.

193
00:20:20,121 --> 00:20:22,857
Put that gun down,
Charlie Blake.

194
00:20:22,957 --> 00:20:24,158
We just come to disarm you.

195
00:20:24,257 --> 00:20:26,426
-Y'all the ones
been hitting them cowtowns

196
00:20:26,527 --> 00:20:27,628
and Shoshone villages

197
00:20:27,729 --> 00:20:29,597
on the Northern trail up
from Nebraska, Charlie?

198
00:20:29,697 --> 00:20:32,466
Huh? don't even bother
robbing 'em no more

199
00:20:32,567 --> 00:20:35,703
you just go
straight to killing 'em?

200
00:20:35,803 --> 00:20:37,237
-I'll tell you square...

201
00:20:37,337 --> 00:20:40,373
This ain't a country
I recognize no more!

202
00:20:40,474 --> 00:20:46,581
White man made to answer
for taking a heathen scalp?!

203
00:20:48,315 --> 00:20:50,785
-Don't you do it, Charlie.

204
00:21:26,254 --> 00:21:29,524
They got me, Dan!

205
00:21:29,624 --> 00:21:34,128
Those cocksuckers got me.

206
00:21:34,494 --> 00:21:37,330
- <i>Christ's sake,</i>
somebody get the Doc!

207
00:22:14,769 --> 00:22:18,039
-Little one can't fall asleep
unless he's with his brother.

208
00:22:18,139 --> 00:22:20,875
Just keeps cryin' and cryin.'

209
00:22:23,244 --> 00:22:25,546
Come on, little one.

210
00:22:26,346 --> 00:22:28,481
- <i>Lucas...</i>

211
00:22:31,319 --> 00:22:33,420
-I wish I could--

212
00:22:34,454 --> 00:22:36,557
We just can't raise up
a little one.

213
00:22:36,657 --> 00:22:39,994
Not with
Mrs. Cochrane's ailments.

214
00:22:40,294 --> 00:22:44,799
-Yeah. That's all right, Bill.

215
00:22:44,899 --> 00:22:46,667
Come on.

216
00:22:55,743 --> 00:22:58,012
- <i>Son of a bitch</i>
<i>calls me on the prod?...</i>

217
00:22:58,112 --> 00:22:59,247
<i>I don't care a continental</i>
<i>that's meant for play...</i>

218
00:22:59,347 --> 00:23:02,216
-Soon as that boy swings,
this one's going in my scabbard

219
00:23:02,316 --> 00:23:04,085
I'll tell you that right now.

220
00:23:04,185 --> 00:23:05,319
You ever seen a filigree
like that?

221
00:23:05,418 --> 00:23:08,789
And hey, what do you figure them
letters is for, huh? That C.R.?

222
00:23:08,890 --> 00:23:11,592
-Shut your damn mouth,
Charlie Culliver!

223
00:23:11,692 --> 00:23:16,564
That ain't but a boy in there,
you addle-headed son of a bitch!

224
00:23:17,131 --> 00:23:18,966
-Okay then, Bill.

225
00:23:22,136 --> 00:23:24,872
-Damnit, I am unwell!

226
00:23:50,197 --> 00:23:52,934
-Can I get you anything, Lucas?

227
00:23:53,834 --> 00:23:55,736
You hungry?

228
00:24:01,441 --> 00:24:03,511
All right.

229
00:25:35,236 --> 00:25:37,271
-You don't look like much.

230
00:25:39,573 --> 00:25:41,342
Come on outta there.

231
00:25:41,442 --> 00:25:43,944
-Mister, I don't know you.

232
00:25:44,311 --> 00:25:46,180
No, no, wait! Sheriff!

233
00:26:31,392 --> 00:26:35,096
-Who the hell's cuttin'
the wolf loose out here?

234
00:26:37,164 --> 00:26:40,334
You get away from that boy,
Mister.

235
00:26:43,204 --> 00:26:45,039
God in Heaven.

236
00:26:48,209 --> 00:26:50,111
-Put it down.

237
00:26:53,747 --> 00:26:56,650
You tell any son of a bitch
who comes after me...

238
00:26:56,750 --> 00:27:00,888
That he will shake hands
with the devil himself.

239
00:27:10,664 --> 00:27:13,602
-Harland-by-God-Rust

240
00:28:01,815 --> 00:28:03,984
-What'd you do to me?

241
00:28:05,620 --> 00:28:08,022
Mister,
what do you want with me?

242
00:28:09,990 --> 00:28:12,860
Did you kill those men?

243
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:15,262
Are you gonna kill me?

244
00:28:30,512 --> 00:28:33,180
I-- I can't leave my brother...

245
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:35,015
I gotta go back.

246
00:28:39,521 --> 00:28:41,722
-There ain't no going back.

247
00:28:44,825 --> 00:28:47,361
We're taking
to the tall timbers.

248
00:28:47,461 --> 00:28:50,665
Straight to the Blackfoot
Highlands til nightfall.

249
00:28:50,764 --> 00:28:52,366
Now you do what I say...

250
00:28:52,466 --> 00:28:56,003
And you might still be alive
when we get there.

251
00:29:02,876 --> 00:29:04,945
-Who are you?

252
00:29:05,779 --> 00:29:07,549
-This ain't no game, boy.

253
00:29:07,649 --> 00:29:09,750
I say ride, we ride,
I say eat, we eat

254
00:29:09,850 --> 00:29:13,087
I say sleep, we sleep.
That's who I am.

255
00:29:14,355 --> 00:29:16,156
Now get on that horse.

256
00:29:33,807 --> 00:29:36,343
-I'm calling for six men
to come forward

257
00:29:36,443 --> 00:29:39,380
and light a shuck
after the Hollister Boy...

258
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:43,652
And that murderous son of a
bitch what shinned out with him.

259
00:29:43,752 --> 00:29:50,991
That's 25 dollars for any man
that posse's up, plus expenses.

260
00:29:56,631 --> 00:29:58,600
Tom Long!

261
00:29:58,700 --> 00:30:00,267
Charlie Culliver!

262
00:30:00,367 --> 00:30:05,072
There's not one man in this town
with the grit to call to account

263
00:30:05,172 --> 00:30:09,443
for what's been done
to these fine men?!

264
00:30:22,590 --> 00:30:25,192
-Drink with me, Marshal!

265
00:30:25,292 --> 00:30:27,094
Tanglefoot Mash.

266
00:30:28,329 --> 00:30:30,097
-Go away.

267
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,770
-Do I offend, Marshal?

268
00:30:35,869 --> 00:30:37,938
Do I cause umbrage?

269
00:30:38,038 --> 00:30:41,108
Does the idea
of bending an elbow

270
00:30:41,208 --> 00:30:46,113
with a Bullwhacker like me
cause recoil?

271
00:30:46,980 --> 00:30:49,183
Is that what you're saying?

272
00:30:51,085 --> 00:30:55,189
-I'm saying
take your air elsewhere.

273
00:31:00,762 --> 00:31:05,866
-Shame them cowboys what got
Buck English and Tom Skinner

274
00:31:05,966 --> 00:31:09,236
wasn't up to task
with you last week.

275
00:31:11,405 --> 00:31:14,074
Wood fucking Helm.

276
00:31:14,642 --> 00:31:18,979
-You just can't shut
the fuck up, can you, huh?!

277
00:31:20,013 --> 00:31:20,948
It ain't in your nature.

278
00:31:21,048 --> 00:31:24,753
-Wood, Wood!...
Hey, buddy, I got you...

279
00:31:24,853 --> 00:31:26,920
Harley, you get the hell
outta here!

280
00:31:27,020 --> 00:31:28,523
Come on, Wood.

281
00:31:28,623 --> 00:31:31,158
-All right, God damnit...

282
00:31:42,804 --> 00:31:45,339
What the fuck
are you all lookin' at?

283
00:31:58,553 --> 00:32:00,588
Et invinies in omnibus...

284
00:32:00,688 --> 00:32:03,691
What the fucking Jesuits
taught me, fucking martyrs...

285
00:32:03,792 --> 00:32:05,560
You know what that means?

286
00:32:07,327 --> 00:32:11,265
You will find God in all things.

287
00:32:12,032 --> 00:32:13,400
That's a good one, ain't it?

288
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:14,401
-Come on,
why don't you get yourself

289
00:32:14,501 --> 00:32:16,336
out of the main thoroughfare,
huh?

290
00:32:16,437 --> 00:32:18,807
You're gonna get yourself hit,
Wood.

291
00:32:18,907 --> 00:32:20,842
-Can you explain to me
where God is

292
00:32:20,941 --> 00:32:23,210
up in that bedroom with my boy?

293
00:32:23,310 --> 00:32:26,614
Can you explain
his part in that to me?

294
00:32:29,684 --> 00:32:33,287
-No, I can't.
I'm sorry, Wood.

295
00:32:35,456 --> 00:32:37,391
The shit I seen...

296
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:40,360
The shit I done.

297
00:32:43,163 --> 00:32:46,701
I knew a long time ago
there ain't no God.

298
00:33:02,082 --> 00:33:04,985
Woulda been nice
to have been wrong though.

299
00:33:30,477 --> 00:33:32,346
-You stay put.

300
00:33:43,925 --> 00:33:45,392
What part of stay put
don't you savvy?

301
00:33:45,492 --> 00:33:48,362
-It ain't even dark yet,
why are we stopping?

302
00:33:50,430 --> 00:33:53,267
-We're gonna sage hen it
right here.

303
00:33:57,605 --> 00:34:00,274
-Who in the hell are you,
mister?

304
00:34:06,113 --> 00:34:09,049
Mister, I asked you a question.

305
00:34:12,152 --> 00:34:13,521
-Name's Rust.

306
00:34:13,621 --> 00:34:16,758
-I ain't ever heard of nobody
called Rust.

307
00:34:17,157 --> 00:34:20,093
-Your ma Wilhelmina
was my little girl.

308
00:34:20,193 --> 00:34:23,865
She run off when she was young
and married your pa.

309
00:34:24,097 --> 00:34:24,933
-That's a damn lie.

310
00:34:25,432 --> 00:34:28,603
My mama didn't have no pa,
said hers died in the war.

311
00:34:29,571 --> 00:34:32,941
-Your ma was a Rust
to the manner born.

312
00:34:33,041 --> 00:34:34,341
Just like you.

313
00:34:34,441 --> 00:34:37,946
That lever belonged
to my Grandaddy Coleman Rust.

314
00:34:38,046 --> 00:34:40,014
He left his mark right there
on the hilt.

315
00:34:40,113 --> 00:34:42,617
-Don't come no closer.

316
00:34:45,687 --> 00:34:47,622
-Give me that rifle, boy.

317
00:34:47,722 --> 00:34:48,723
-You're a murderer.

318
00:34:48,823 --> 00:34:52,560
-Well, that's something
we have in common.

319
00:34:55,395 --> 00:34:57,031
-You can go to hell.

320
00:34:57,130 --> 00:34:58,633
-Next time you wanna
kill somebody,

321
00:34:58,733 --> 00:35:01,836
you make sure you lever one
in there.

322
00:35:03,170 --> 00:35:05,673
-Go twice then for all I care.

323
00:35:09,209 --> 00:35:11,713
-First one's gentle.

324
00:35:11,813 --> 00:35:14,114
Next one won't be.

325
00:35:22,624 --> 00:35:25,292
-What were you looking at
up there?

326
00:35:28,362 --> 00:35:31,032
-This is Shoshone territory.

327
00:35:31,131 --> 00:35:34,267
That scrub cypress
there's a warning sign.

328
00:35:34,368 --> 00:35:36,704
What's left of the
Northern Shoshone been warring

329
00:35:36,804 --> 00:35:37,972
with the settlement militia

330
00:35:38,072 --> 00:35:42,175
all up and down the Big Horn
Plateau ever since Bear River.

331
00:35:42,275 --> 00:35:44,746
Be a shame if we wandered
onto their territory

332
00:35:44,846 --> 00:35:48,116
and they mistook us
for Syracuse Minutemen

333
00:35:48,215 --> 00:35:50,551
and we ended up losing
our scalps.

334
00:35:50,652 --> 00:35:53,588
We'll go around 'em
in the morning.

335
00:35:54,254 --> 00:35:56,858
Anybody ever teach you
to set a snare?

336
00:35:56,958 --> 00:35:58,492
-Yeah.

337
00:36:01,029 --> 00:36:02,930
-Let's go then.

338
00:36:10,705 --> 00:36:12,874
Trail coming
outta the briar patch,

339
00:36:12,974 --> 00:36:15,175
you look close.

340
00:36:30,591 --> 00:36:32,359
Hold this.

341
00:36:36,064 --> 00:36:38,566
-Have you ever seen a man hang?

342
00:36:38,833 --> 00:36:40,668
- <i>Once or twice.</i>

343
00:36:42,870 --> 00:36:44,872
-What was it like?

344
00:36:44,972 --> 00:36:47,809
-Ain't the kind of thing
a man should dwell on.

345
00:36:57,952 --> 00:36:59,821
Skin this.

346
00:37:01,055 --> 00:37:03,825
Then throw him on the fire.

347
00:37:22,577 --> 00:37:24,277
-Elwood.

348
00:37:25,312 --> 00:37:28,549
Laurence.

349
00:37:30,383 --> 00:37:32,319
Thank you.

350
00:37:34,922 --> 00:37:36,224
God damn.

351
00:37:36,323 --> 00:37:39,259
-You're the one made it,
I'd reckon.

352
00:37:39,727 --> 00:37:41,996
-I miss your telegram, Laurence?

353
00:37:42,096 --> 00:37:43,698
-Just rode in this morning.

354
00:37:43,798 --> 00:37:46,601
What's the salt up
in Hayesville?

355
00:37:47,235 --> 00:37:48,268
-A man come to town,

356
00:37:48,368 --> 00:37:50,505
kill't Tom Long
and two Deputies...

357
00:37:50,605 --> 00:37:54,642
Sprung the boy, what I
understand he didn't go willing.

358
00:37:54,742 --> 00:37:56,611
-Harland Rust.

359
00:37:57,444 --> 00:37:59,614
-So they claim.

360
00:38:00,815 --> 00:38:04,852
-The same Harland Rust
what murdered Hick Roberts

361
00:38:04,952 --> 00:38:06,854
up in Lincoln back in '67...

362
00:38:06,954 --> 00:38:10,091
Dynamited all them banks up
and down Arkansas,

363
00:38:10,191 --> 00:38:12,593
what was that, '72?

364
00:38:12,693 --> 00:38:13,795
-Yeah.

365
00:38:13,895 --> 00:38:16,564
Done that robbery down
in Crowley too.

366
00:38:16,664 --> 00:38:19,332
1868,
him and the Alvord Stiles Gang,

367
00:38:19,432 --> 00:38:20,868
killed five men.

368
00:38:20,968 --> 00:38:23,938
If I had to guess, he's headed
for the Southern Plains.

369
00:38:24,038 --> 00:38:24,972
- <i>Injun territory.</i>

370
00:38:25,072 --> 00:38:26,941
-Yeah. Settlement's are scarce.

371
00:38:27,041 --> 00:38:30,878
Only jurisdiction belongs
to the U.S. Government.

372
00:38:31,112 --> 00:38:34,347
The boy had an Aunt on his
Mother's side come calling

373
00:38:34,447 --> 00:38:36,684
on his behalf two days prior.

374
00:38:36,784 --> 00:38:40,254
Evelyn Bassett,
up from Sheridan County.

375
00:38:40,353 --> 00:38:42,623
-That mean something?

376
00:38:43,291 --> 00:38:45,458
-Probably it don't.

377
00:38:45,760 --> 00:38:47,562
-I want this son of a bitch,
Wood.

378
00:38:47,662 --> 00:38:48,563
It's been going on eight years

379
00:38:48,663 --> 00:38:50,565
since anyone's seen hide
nor hair.

380
00:38:50,665 --> 00:38:53,668
I'll give you men, resources,
whatever you need.

381
00:38:53,768 --> 00:38:55,402
-Be best if I travel light.

382
00:38:55,503 --> 00:38:56,604
-At least take
Dick Miller along.

383
00:38:56,704 --> 00:38:58,172
He's gonna be riding
in this afternoon.

384
00:38:58,272 --> 00:38:59,507
-Christ's sake, Laurence...

385
00:39:00,141 --> 00:39:01,642
-If it's getting to where you
can't throw a rope out there

386
00:39:01,742 --> 00:39:02,810
without catching it on someone

387
00:39:02,910 --> 00:39:05,345
I'd prefer you had more backup
than just Drum

388
00:39:05,445 --> 00:39:08,649
and them two Shitkickers
out of Atchison.

389
00:39:09,750 --> 00:39:12,854
I never met nobody
hunted a man like you, Wood.

390
00:39:12,954 --> 00:39:16,724
Never met nobody who kept
files and used forensics

391
00:39:16,824 --> 00:39:17,457
and whatnot

392
00:39:17,959 --> 00:39:19,994
instead of just relying
on good old fashioned pursuit

393
00:39:20,094 --> 00:39:21,963
and capture.

394
00:39:24,298 --> 00:39:26,701
How's your boy?

395
00:39:34,275 --> 00:39:36,677
All right then, Wood.

396
00:40:32,633 --> 00:40:36,003
-You just got yourself killed,
boy.

397
00:40:36,671 --> 00:40:38,906
You really think you stand
some kind of a chance

398
00:40:39,006 --> 00:40:43,945
out here alone,
instead of with me?

399
00:40:45,746 --> 00:40:48,849
You know what happens
when a man hangs?

400
00:40:48,950 --> 00:40:51,752
If he's lucky, his neck
snaps clean and that's that.

401
00:40:51,852 --> 00:40:56,791
And if'n he ain't, well...
he dangles for a spell.

402
00:40:57,058 --> 00:40:59,794
Messes his trousers,
eyes pop out,

403
00:40:59,894 --> 00:41:03,664
go coal black
while he chokes to death...

404
00:41:04,565 --> 00:41:07,068
Might not die
straight away neither.

405
00:41:07,168 --> 00:41:09,537
Might take an hour...

406
00:41:09,971 --> 00:41:11,639
Or two.

407
00:41:11,739 --> 00:41:17,111
You really in such an all-fire
hurry to back to that?!

408
00:41:19,046 --> 00:41:20,948
-What do you care?

409
00:41:24,785 --> 00:41:26,187
-I'll tell you what...

410
00:41:26,287 --> 00:41:30,992
You show me all the folks
you got lined up that do,

411
00:41:32,626 --> 00:41:35,863
and I'll leave you be.

412
00:42:55,743 --> 00:42:57,512
-It's a Godless thing,

413
00:42:57,611 --> 00:43:00,948
keeping a man
from burial like this.

414
00:43:04,285 --> 00:43:06,120
-You can bury him now.

415
00:43:11,792 --> 00:43:15,463
-You sure you don't wanna
stop off any place else, Wood?

416
00:43:15,564 --> 00:43:18,332
I'm sure Rust would appreciate
getting out of Wyoming quick

417
00:43:18,432 --> 00:43:20,301
as we can let him.

418
00:43:24,238 --> 00:43:26,607
-Shut your cockholster.

419
00:43:42,524 --> 00:43:44,925
-You don't look like her.

420
00:43:46,994 --> 00:43:50,397
Her manner wasn't nothing
like yours neither.

421
00:43:51,699 --> 00:43:54,335
My mother was a spirited woman.

422
00:44:02,143 --> 00:44:04,945
My pa used to say a man
that looks over his shoulder

423
00:44:05,045 --> 00:44:06,013
on a straight piece of road

424
00:44:06,113 --> 00:44:09,316
ain't a man
that led an honest life.

425
00:44:13,220 --> 00:44:17,324
Might as well be talking to your
horse as much as you got to say.

426
00:44:19,460 --> 00:44:22,429
Better traveling companion too.

427
00:44:22,963 --> 00:44:25,266
-He doesn't ask
as many questions as you do,

428
00:44:25,366 --> 00:44:27,434
I'll give him that.

429
00:44:28,637 --> 00:44:30,671
Let's stop here.

430
00:44:40,549 --> 00:44:42,683
Ha!

431
00:44:46,854 --> 00:44:48,389
-What'd you do that for?

432
00:44:48,489 --> 00:44:52,359
-He was spent.
You could tell from his breath.

433
00:44:52,459 --> 00:44:56,497
Panic'll take hold and he'll run
for miles then he'll drop.

434
00:44:56,598 --> 00:45:00,669
Anyone coming for us'll have
to account for those tracks.

435
00:45:00,768 --> 00:45:03,003
We'll ride two up.

436
00:45:04,506 --> 00:45:06,608
-I don't know what to call you.

437
00:45:06,707 --> 00:45:08,142
- <i>Call me how you like.</i>

438
00:45:08,242 --> 00:45:10,811
-Will you at least tell me
where you're taking me?

439
00:45:10,911 --> 00:45:15,584
-New Mexico. South of the
Mescalero Reservation,

440
00:45:15,684 --> 00:45:17,652
town called Masilla.

441
00:45:17,751 --> 00:45:19,453
-What's in Masilla?

442
00:45:19,554 --> 00:45:21,021
-Man, I used to ride with.

443
00:45:21,121 --> 00:45:23,490
I send word, he'll take us
to the Mexican side

444
00:45:23,592 --> 00:45:24,825
of El Paso, Guadalupe.

445
00:45:24,925 --> 00:45:26,528
There's an
Anglican school there.

446
00:45:26,628 --> 00:45:29,129
-I can't speak Spanish.

447
00:45:29,698 --> 00:45:32,199
-So we should go back
to Hayesville?

448
00:45:34,735 --> 00:45:36,337
These folks are from up North.

449
00:45:36,437 --> 00:45:40,975
Teach wetbacks how to speak
English proper and the like.

450
00:45:41,075 --> 00:45:44,011
No lawman North of El Paso
can come for you...

451
00:45:44,111 --> 00:45:46,113
No bounty hunter would think
to look there either.

452
00:45:46,213 --> 00:45:48,849
-I don't want to go to Mexico.

453
00:45:49,783 --> 00:45:52,119
-Want don't enter into it.

454
00:45:55,690 --> 00:46:01,529
There's alive and there's ain't.
Try to focus on the former.

455
00:46:01,795 --> 00:46:05,933
-What about you?
Will you stay in Mexico?

456
00:46:06,267 --> 00:46:09,303
-The food don't set with me.
Come on.

457
00:46:12,840 --> 00:46:18,145
-She never mentioned you.
My Mother, not once.

458
00:46:18,513 --> 00:46:20,515
- <i>I expect.</i>

459
00:46:42,570 --> 00:46:43,638
- <i>Tolliver.</i>

460
00:46:43,738 --> 00:46:45,939
-Preacher!

461
00:46:47,975 --> 00:46:51,211
Christ,
look at this sorry rawheel.

462
00:46:51,312 --> 00:46:54,915
-Man from the railroad'll be
by tomorrow to collect him...

463
00:46:55,015 --> 00:46:58,085
Take him back to Missouri
to hang.

464
00:46:58,952 --> 00:47:01,623
-Now what's an old reb like you

465
00:47:01,723 --> 00:47:04,458
doing this West of Kentucky
anyhow?

466
00:47:04,559 --> 00:47:07,562
- Fuckin' your mother.

467
00:47:09,129 --> 00:47:12,966
-Oh, a telegram come in
for you.

468
00:47:13,067 --> 00:47:16,604
Thousand dollar bounty
just went out.

469
00:47:17,037 --> 00:47:20,742
That name mean anything to you,
Harland Rust?

470
00:47:20,841 --> 00:47:23,844
He is the formidable sort.

471
00:47:24,211 --> 00:47:27,981
-To merit a thousand dollar's
I'd reckon so.

472
00:47:28,817 --> 00:47:31,452
God bless the wicked.

473
00:47:32,052 --> 00:47:33,921
For they continue
to pay my bills.

474
00:47:43,698 --> 00:47:47,334
-Come on. Come on...

475
00:47:47,434 --> 00:47:49,336
Don't be scared...

476
00:47:49,571 --> 00:47:51,606
Don't be scared now.

477
00:47:57,645 --> 00:47:58,979
-Hey.

478
00:47:59,079 --> 00:48:01,915
- <i>Come on.</i>
<i>Hey, you got it.</i>

479
00:48:02,015 --> 00:48:03,718
-Hey, shithead.

480
00:48:03,818 --> 00:48:04,719
-Hey!

481
00:48:04,819 --> 00:48:07,655
The devil what stuck me
with you!

482
00:48:07,756 --> 00:48:10,357
-Yonder come three riders.

483
00:48:19,734 --> 00:48:21,935
State your business!

484
00:48:22,035 --> 00:48:23,270
-Boone. Clete.

485
00:48:23,370 --> 00:48:25,807
You're lookin' prosperous
as usual.

486
00:48:25,906 --> 00:48:28,942
-Wood Helm. Drum.

487
00:48:29,042 --> 00:48:31,011
What the hell you doin'
out here?

488
00:48:31,111 --> 00:48:33,080
-We're traking
a couple fugitives headed South.

489
00:48:33,180 --> 00:48:36,417
Man and a young boy, could use
you if you wanna ride along.

490
00:48:36,518 --> 00:48:40,120
-I don't know, Wood.
We got these hogs now.

491
00:48:40,220 --> 00:48:44,024
-Could pay you
200 each plus expenses.

492
00:48:44,425 --> 00:48:48,295
You still uh... you still
making that Lagu Pierre beef?

493
00:48:48,395 --> 00:48:49,329
-I sure am.

494
00:48:49,430 --> 00:48:51,365
Little clarified butter
in the pan...

495
00:48:51,465 --> 00:48:54,636
Rosemary, I'll splash in
some of that Medeira.

496
00:48:54,736 --> 00:48:58,472
I must confess, I've been
trying my hand at a nice

497
00:48:58,573 --> 00:49:01,743
vol au vent
fianciere type pastry too.

498
00:49:01,843 --> 00:49:03,377
-Main ingredient's bullshit.

499
00:49:03,477 --> 00:49:04,044
-Bite your tongue!

500
00:49:04,144 --> 00:49:06,213
Civilized men are conversatin.'

501
00:49:06,313 --> 00:49:08,817
-So what do you say?
You wanna come with?

502
00:49:08,917 --> 00:49:12,687
