If brains was knives
you couldn't cut hot butter.

750
01:11:42,937 --> 01:11:44,906
That's good cornmeal
you're wasting.

751
01:11:45,006 --> 01:11:45,973
-Do you take umbrage?

752
01:11:46,073 --> 01:11:47,542
-You takin' umbrage?

753
01:11:47,642 --> 01:11:52,513
l'air n'est-il pas charmant à
cette de la journée?.

754
01:11:52,613 --> 01:11:56,517
Isn't the sky lovely
this time of day?

755
01:11:56,617 --> 01:11:57,819
Yeah.

756
01:11:57,919 --> 01:12:01,055
You're wasting it again,
I'm warning you, Clete.

757
01:12:01,556 --> 01:12:04,959
-Do you take umbrage?
-You take umbrage?

758
01:12:05,059 --> 01:12:08,596
Defend yourself,
you muley lipped cocksucker!

759
01:12:08,696 --> 01:12:10,665
Hiya!

760
01:12:15,335 --> 01:12:17,004
Grease bellied cocksucker
I will do you harm!

761
01:12:17,104 --> 01:12:19,574
- <i>Hey God damnit.</i>
Knock that shit off.

762
01:12:19,674 --> 01:12:21,042
<i>I'm gonna beat you to a pulp!</i>

763
01:12:21,142 --> 01:12:24,377
-You know, we ain't got time
for such nonsense.

764
01:12:24,477 --> 01:12:26,681
By all means.

765
01:12:27,281 --> 01:12:29,884
<i>You take umbrage?! Huh?!</i>

766
01:12:29,984 --> 01:12:32,253
<i>I'm tired of your shit!</i>

767
01:12:39,327 --> 01:12:42,230
-I said pull in your horns
God damnit, now!

768
01:12:42,330 --> 01:12:43,731
-I wouldn't do that
if I was you, no,

769
01:12:43,831 --> 01:12:45,398
that's just gonna rile him up.

770
01:12:45,498 --> 01:12:46,734
This one bucks close
to the ground,

771
01:12:46,834 --> 01:12:49,303
he'll fight you
til hell freezes over.

772
01:12:49,402 --> 01:12:51,305
Then he'll skate on the ice.

773
01:12:51,404 --> 01:12:54,175
-Then what would you recommend,
Drum?

774
01:12:54,275 --> 01:12:55,309
-I don't know, Miller.

775
01:12:55,408 --> 01:12:58,346
You're the one
that got off your horse.

776
01:12:58,445 --> 01:12:59,881
-Hey, Boone.

777
01:13:03,985 --> 01:13:08,022
Don't make me tell your ma
you two was scrappin.'

778
01:13:38,819 --> 01:13:40,254
-Yeah...

779
01:13:40,354 --> 01:13:42,556
Dead as corned beef these two.

780
01:13:42,657 --> 01:13:45,793
-A couple Apache come
across 'em, brung 'em here.

781
01:13:45,893 --> 01:13:47,628
County'll pay
20 dollars per so

782
01:13:47,728 --> 01:13:50,598
as to discourage folk
from trading the teeth

783
01:13:50,698 --> 01:13:52,566
and the eyeballs
and the like.

784
01:13:52,667 --> 01:13:55,269
Blue River trail area, you say?

785
01:13:55,369 --> 01:13:57,204
-That dugout hollow
in that dog leg,

786
01:13:57,305 --> 01:14:00,141
two day's ride from Windy Hill.

787
01:14:00,241 --> 01:14:01,609
-Oh yeah...

788
01:14:01,709 --> 01:14:03,077
Got a little bite to it.

789
01:14:03,177 --> 01:14:04,211
See here?

790
01:14:04,345 --> 01:14:07,515
Bowie knife. Got them jagged
little teeth on the spine.

791
01:14:07,615 --> 01:14:13,187
Same pigsticker kill't Tom Long,
I had to venture a guess.

792
01:14:16,524 --> 01:14:19,527
-Buzzards startin'
to gather out yonder.

793
01:14:19,627 --> 01:14:21,494
-What do you mean?

794
01:14:21,829 --> 01:14:26,033
-Scavengers.
They come for the bodies.

795
01:14:26,133 --> 01:14:27,568
-The hell you say.

796
01:14:27,668 --> 01:14:29,437
-Fella from the county's
supposed to come out

797
01:14:29,537 --> 01:14:30,771
with the mail wagon Wednesday...

798
01:14:30,871 --> 01:14:34,608
Take them trappers
and the post on to Garfield.

799
01:14:34,842 --> 01:14:38,179
Looks like them fellers
ain't gonna wait.

800
01:14:40,181 --> 01:14:42,149
-Say hello, Clete.

801
01:14:58,432 --> 01:15:00,534
-Damn, Clete, you could back
a buzzard off a gut wagon,

802
01:15:00,634 --> 01:15:03,004
but that was a damn fine shot.

803
01:15:03,104 --> 01:15:04,372
-God damn wind kicked up,

804
01:15:04,472 --> 01:15:06,807
otherwise I'd have taken the
feather right off that bowler.

805
01:15:06,907 --> 01:15:12,046
-Well... Goodbye old paint,
for I am leaving Cheyenne.

806
01:15:17,051 --> 01:15:21,222
-Got an appetite like a Coyote
for a little scrap.

807
01:15:21,455 --> 01:15:24,291
Like having a third man
riding along.

808
01:15:31,132 --> 01:15:33,134
You all right?

809
01:15:34,435 --> 01:15:37,238
-I was just thinking
about my Mother.

810
01:15:37,972 --> 01:15:41,008
It's funny, I can remember every
single thing about her dying

811
01:15:41,108 --> 01:15:43,744
but I can't seem
to remember her face.

812
01:15:43,844 --> 01:15:48,883
-It's hard watching someone
getting taken slow like that.

813
01:15:50,317 --> 01:15:53,087
-I was the one
kept care of her.

814
01:15:53,687 --> 01:15:57,958
Think I was ten maybe,
Jacob was barely walking yet.

815
01:15:58,859 --> 01:16:03,664
The fever just kept taking
little parts of her day by day.

816
01:16:04,665 --> 01:16:05,800
-Let's eat up.

817
01:16:05,900 --> 01:16:08,869
Got a long day's ride
ahead of us tomorrow.

818
01:16:08,969 --> 01:16:13,040
We keep up a good tilt, we'll
make New Mexico by nightfall.

819
01:16:16,143 --> 01:16:18,245
-What happened to you?

820
01:16:20,549 --> 01:16:22,416
-How do you mean?

821
01:16:22,583 --> 01:16:25,086
Why are you so full of hate?

822
01:16:26,353 --> 01:16:29,256
You know where I'm from?

823
01:16:29,356 --> 01:16:30,291
-Wyoming?

824
01:16:35,296 --> 01:16:37,498
I'm from Chicago.

825
01:16:37,598 --> 01:16:39,233
-No.
-Yeah.

826
01:16:39,333 --> 01:16:43,504
My father was a newspaper man,
Harland Senior.

827
01:16:43,704 --> 01:16:45,406
After my time
with the Fifth Regiment,

828
01:16:45,507 --> 01:16:46,607
I come down to Oklahoma to farm

829
01:16:46,841 --> 01:16:51,712
had me a hundred acre corn,
another fifty hard durum...

830
01:16:51,979 --> 01:16:54,882
We got flooded out in '65...

831
01:16:55,116 --> 01:16:58,252
Smith Norton Bank
took my land...

832
01:16:59,854 --> 01:17:03,924
I dynamited those sons
of bitches in '66.

833
01:17:04,391 --> 01:17:09,230
And two more banks up
the Ottawa Trail in '67.

834
01:17:11,065 --> 01:17:13,134
I have not been
on speaking terms

835
01:17:13,234 --> 01:17:16,003
with the law ever since.

836
01:17:16,470 --> 01:17:20,341
My grandfather Coleman Rust,
he fought in the Apache Wars...

837
01:17:20,441 --> 01:17:25,312
Kill't himself 38 Apaches
using this very rifle.

838
01:17:26,013 --> 01:17:29,183
Used to stay with us
when I was a boy.

839
01:17:29,283 --> 01:17:34,455
Taught me the Ozark
back county. Jicarilla.

840
01:17:34,556 --> 01:17:38,359
How to stalk deer
in the Chautauqua Hills.

841
01:17:39,426 --> 01:17:41,829
That cedar line...

842
01:17:43,998 --> 01:17:47,268
Like hunting a whisper
in the wind.

843
01:17:48,235 --> 01:17:52,574
Not much paw and heller in that
anymore, not for an old man.

844
01:17:52,673 --> 01:17:56,010
I mostly go
from place to place now.

845
01:17:56,110 --> 01:18:01,282
Worked as a Brakeman...
Run mustangs in the Dakotas...

846
01:18:01,382 --> 01:18:04,285
Mule skinner, foundryman...

847
01:18:04,653 --> 01:18:06,787
-Must get lonely.

848
01:18:08,322 --> 01:18:10,791
-A man makes his choices.

849
01:18:12,826 --> 01:18:14,862
-Did you know?

850
01:18:15,597 --> 01:18:17,331
About my mother I mean?

851
01:18:17,431 --> 01:18:22,102
-I heard something last August,
I dont know...

852
01:18:22,203 --> 01:18:25,706
I always thought
I'd have a chance to...

853
01:18:29,443 --> 01:18:33,414
Some things in this life
you can't get back, I reckon.

854
01:18:45,726 --> 01:18:48,229
- <i>Hey! Get back here!</i>

855
01:18:51,198 --> 01:18:52,967
<i>Come here!</i>

856
01:19:06,615 --> 01:19:08,282
-Whoa...

857
01:19:09,783 --> 01:19:11,452
-What's all the bother?

858
01:19:11,553 --> 01:19:13,220
-It's that reward went out.

859
01:19:13,320 --> 01:19:16,156
-Bunch of ditch riders and mail
order cowboys couldn't find

860
01:19:16,257 --> 01:19:18,359
their ass with two hands,
you ask me.

861
01:19:18,459 --> 01:19:19,093
Who's the reward on?

862
01:19:19,193 --> 01:19:20,427
-Somebody thought
they mighta seen

863
01:19:20,528 --> 01:19:21,563
that Hollister boy yesterday

864
01:19:21,663 --> 01:19:24,365
while they was hangin'
Henry Pickett.

865
01:19:24,465 --> 01:19:25,634
Him and Harland Rust.

866
01:19:25,734 --> 01:19:28,703
Thousand dollars out
on the both of 'em.

867
01:19:28,802 --> 01:19:30,037
Bunch of hell for leather types

868
01:19:30,137 --> 01:19:33,207
have been coming
through here steady since.

869
01:19:33,541 --> 01:19:36,010
-Thousand dollars, you say?

870
01:19:36,110 --> 01:19:38,145
Well...
Time to swap some lead

871
01:19:38,245 --> 01:19:41,516
and have ourselves
a horse race, I suppose.

872
01:20:09,678 --> 01:20:11,812
-We best get a drag on.

873
01:20:12,446 --> 01:20:16,116
-He used to go on and on
about this rifle.

874
01:20:17,484 --> 01:20:18,986
My pa.

875
01:20:19,286 --> 01:20:20,522
He'd strip it down every week,

876
01:20:20,622 --> 01:20:23,924
polish everything all the way
down to the springs.

877
01:20:25,560 --> 01:20:26,561
This Henry...

878
01:20:27,294 --> 01:20:30,799
It's ruined the life of almost
anyone it's ever come across.

879
01:20:30,998 --> 01:20:35,836
Them Apaches... mine,
Charles Gantry's...

880
01:20:38,573 --> 01:20:40,341
My father's.

881
01:20:40,441 --> 01:20:42,176
-How do you mean?

882
01:20:43,877 --> 01:20:45,212
- <i>He killed himself</i>
<i>with this rifle</i>

883
01:20:45,312 --> 01:20:48,082
<i>a year after my mother passed.</i>

884
01:20:56,725 --> 01:20:58,859
-You're lookin' poorly.

885
01:21:00,494 --> 01:21:02,162
Gettin' ready to boil.

886
01:21:02,262 --> 01:21:06,100
Man I used to ride with about
a half day North of Arnett.

887
01:21:06,200 --> 01:21:10,971
We'll go stay with him.
Come on.

888
01:21:39,500 --> 01:21:41,201
Your pa about?

889
01:21:42,169 --> 01:21:44,104
-What do you want?

890
01:21:44,271 --> 01:21:46,974
-Lookin' for Chunk Bowdre.

891
01:21:48,510 --> 01:21:51,011
-I remember you.

892
01:21:52,547 --> 01:21:54,381
Figured you for dead.

893
01:21:54,481 --> 01:21:55,617
- <i>Chunk about?</i>

894
01:21:55,717 --> 01:21:57,585
-You're five years too late.

895
01:21:57,685 --> 01:22:00,722
Bunch of men in hoods
come for him one night

896
01:22:00,822 --> 01:22:04,191
for something y'all done up
in Nebraska 20 years ago.

897
01:22:04,291 --> 01:22:09,129
They strung him up from that
Mexican Blue Oak out yonder.

898
01:22:09,229 --> 01:22:13,601
Hoping they mighta' found what
rock you was hiding under too.

899
01:22:13,701 --> 01:22:14,869
-The boy needs a bed.

900
01:22:14,968 --> 01:22:18,338
-Ain't no bed here.
Not for you.

901
01:22:18,439 --> 01:22:23,210
Not for any of you murdering
bastards ever run with Chunk.

902
01:22:26,681 --> 01:22:27,682
-My condolences.

903
01:22:28,182 --> 01:22:31,018
-You can take your condolences
the hell outta here.

904
01:22:31,118 --> 01:22:34,087
And don't never come back.

905
01:22:40,060 --> 01:22:42,597
-You look after him, all right?

906
01:22:59,814 --> 01:23:01,448
-Appreciate it.

907
01:23:02,082 --> 01:23:03,183
-Frank Bascom.

908
01:23:03,283 --> 01:23:05,954
You old alkalied mule,
how you keepin?'

909
01:23:06,053 --> 01:23:06,921
Wood Helm.

910
01:23:07,755 --> 01:23:10,592
Well I don't travel like a Colt
no more but I ain't complaining.

911
01:23:10,692 --> 01:23:12,125
- <i>I was wondering</i>
<i>if you still had</i>

912
01:23:12,226 --> 01:23:14,529
<i>that old 40 rod Sharps...</i>

913
01:23:14,629 --> 01:23:16,263
<i>Heading into</i>
unorganized territory

914
01:23:16,363 --> 01:23:18,265
<i>and I'd like to have something</i>
<i>with a little more range</i>

915
01:23:18,365 --> 01:23:21,502
<i>than that old</i>
<i>Remington Rolling Block.</i>

916
01:23:21,603 --> 01:23:26,340
-Laurence Stilwell sent word
from Ledford...

917
01:23:26,608 --> 01:23:30,210
Fella from the telegraph office
brung it over.

918
01:23:33,146 --> 01:23:35,315
I'm sorry, Wood.

919
01:23:45,158 --> 01:23:47,227
-All right then.

920
01:24:21,930 --> 01:24:23,598
-Hey whoa...

921
01:24:23,998 --> 01:24:24,866
-Lucas...

922
01:24:24,966 --> 01:24:27,167
Whoa... Whoa whoa...

923
01:24:55,530 --> 01:24:57,297
Hah!

924
01:25:13,180 --> 01:25:16,017
-Shhhh...

925
01:25:16,116 --> 01:25:18,118
Be still now.

926
01:25:18,485 --> 01:25:20,521
-I don't think it's Typhoid.

927
01:25:20,622 --> 01:25:23,490
Cholera neither,
his back ain't all rigid

928
01:25:23,591 --> 01:25:28,462
and I don't see no spots.
I got some things here...

929
01:25:28,563 --> 01:25:34,769
see if I can make something
maybe to break his fever.

930
01:25:36,269 --> 01:25:38,840
-I'm sorry...

931
01:25:39,607 --> 01:25:41,509
Mama...

932
01:25:41,609 --> 01:25:44,045
-Quiet now...

933
01:25:44,144 --> 01:25:46,179
-I'm sorry!...

934
01:25:46,781 --> 01:25:48,783
Mama!...

935
01:25:58,225 --> 01:25:59,292
-He is as ugly as homemade sin,

936
01:25:59,393 --> 01:26:01,095
but he knows
how to toss them pots around

937
01:26:01,228 --> 01:26:03,296
I will give him that.

938
01:26:03,397 --> 01:26:06,100
-Old Boone's outdone
himself again.

939
01:26:06,199 --> 01:26:07,568
Made some nice squab chicken...

940
01:26:07,669 --> 01:26:10,404
some of these
fried parsnip cakes...

941
01:26:10,504 --> 01:26:13,306
Little milk butter on 'em...

942
01:26:15,375 --> 01:26:16,611
You oughta eat something, Wood.

943
01:26:16,711 --> 01:26:19,747
-No I'm good.
Look, look. Look here, look...

944
01:26:19,847 --> 01:26:23,417
Little town called Mosquero,
other side of Dawes Pass...

945
01:26:23,518 --> 01:26:26,253
Only place for a hundred miles
Rust can supply up

946
01:26:26,353 --> 01:26:28,188
before he heads South.

947
01:26:28,288 --> 01:26:31,025
I figure he'll be there
in two days' time.

948
01:26:31,125 --> 01:26:32,492
Liable to be too many folks
on the trail

949
01:26:32,593 --> 01:26:34,762
so he's gonna head right up
over this pass

950
01:26:34,862 --> 01:26:36,396
Now we stick to the trail,

951
01:26:36,496 --> 01:26:39,433
we'll beat him there
by half a day.

952
01:26:39,867 --> 01:26:43,771
First chance we get,
I'll send word to Stilwell.

953
01:26:45,173 --> 01:26:48,943
-Maybe we oughta
wait a minute, Wood.

954
01:26:51,311 --> 01:26:55,516
-You know it occurs to me
that I...

955
01:26:55,616 --> 01:26:58,886
I've survived just
about every lawman I ever...

956
01:26:58,986 --> 01:27:01,288
I ever worked with.

957
01:27:01,388 --> 01:27:04,092
You realize that, Drum?

958
01:27:04,192 --> 01:27:06,961
-Don't put me
in the ground just yet.

959
01:27:07,061 --> 01:27:14,234
-Apprehended 146 wanted men
in my career as a U.S. Marshal.

960
01:27:14,334 --> 01:27:17,772
- <i>Yeah?</i>
-18 of 'em I sent to hang.

961
01:27:19,306 --> 01:27:21,709
-Never did no damn good neither.

962
01:27:21,809 --> 01:27:25,412
Certainly never seemed
to deter nobody.

963
01:27:27,548 --> 01:27:30,184
- <i>Well the only order</i>
that exists in this world

964
01:27:30,283 --> 01:27:31,652
<i>is the order we impose.</i>

965
01:27:31,753 --> 01:27:35,656
<i>A man loses sight of that,</i>
he's got nothing.

966
01:27:36,023 --> 01:27:38,559
<i>You taught me that.</i>

967
01:27:39,761 --> 01:27:42,029
-Last year,
I brought Tom Bell his self,

968
01:27:42,130 --> 01:27:44,464
head of the Tom Bell Gang
to justice

969
01:27:44,565 --> 01:27:48,569
for killing them two fellers
in Marysville.

970
01:27:49,771 --> 01:27:54,341
When they asked Tom his
final words up on that scaffold,

971
01:27:54,441 --> 01:27:56,711
he spoke with a peace

972
01:27:56,811 --> 01:28:00,548
and a clarity I'd never heard
from a man.

973
01:28:03,050 --> 01:28:04,519
Here's a man
for whom the long,

974
01:28:04,619 --> 01:28:07,755
hard road was finally over...

975
01:28:08,388 --> 01:28:10,825
And it was with certainty
he was going off

976
01:28:10,925 --> 01:28:13,594
to meet his great reward.

977
01:28:16,531 --> 01:28:19,499
But the second they pulled
that lever,

978
01:28:20,467 --> 01:28:22,603
I knew that was it.

979
01:28:23,938 --> 01:28:27,875
There was no great reward
waiting on Tom.

980
01:28:31,078 --> 01:28:33,881
Just eternity of nothing.

981
01:28:35,950 --> 01:28:39,053
And that's all a man gets
in this world.

982
01:28:44,625 --> 01:28:47,028
Eight years old, Drum.

983
01:29:13,821 --> 01:29:15,690
- <i>Lucas...</i>

984
01:29:30,905 --> 01:29:32,673
<i>Lucas...</i>

985
01:29:32,807 --> 01:29:36,844
<i>Lucas!</i>

986
01:29:58,366 --> 01:30:00,735
-See you got
some of your color back.

987
01:30:07,174 --> 01:30:09,510
-How long was I out for?

988
01:30:10,544 --> 01:30:11,579
-Day and a half.

989
01:30:12,179 --> 01:30:15,583
You were in and out for most
of it til the fever broke.

990
01:30:17,718 --> 01:30:19,452
-Thanks.

991
01:30:56,190 --> 01:30:59,160
-That's a fine pup
you got there, little man.

992
01:30:59,260 --> 01:31:01,796
- <i>His name's Albert.</i>

993
01:31:03,496 --> 01:31:04,432
-How long you had him?

994
01:31:04,899 --> 01:31:07,401
- <i>Two days.</i>
Boy and his grandpa come by.

995
01:31:07,500 --> 01:31:09,270
<i>Boy let me keep him.</i>

996
01:31:09,370 --> 01:31:11,439
-Well ain't that a treat.

997
01:31:11,539 --> 01:31:14,208
A boy and his grandpa you say.

998
01:31:14,442 --> 01:31:17,178
<i>Samuel, who you talkin' to?</i>

999
01:31:18,446 --> 01:31:22,482
-Afternoon Ma'am.
Name's Fenton Lang.

1000
01:31:22,583 --> 01:31:25,019
Won't ask for
but a minute of your time.

1001
01:31:25,119 --> 01:31:26,287
-You from the bank?

1002
01:31:26,387 --> 01:31:28,289
- <i>No, Ma'am.</i>

1003
01:31:28,389 --> 01:31:29,390
-We ain't lookin' to sell.

1004
01:31:29,489 --> 01:31:33,027
-Well, Ma'am,
I wouldn't dream of asking.

1005
01:31:33,627 --> 01:31:35,896
You're widow to Chunk Bowdre,
that right?

1006
01:31:35,997 --> 01:31:39,499
Heard he'd been took a
few years back, my condolences.

1007
01:31:39,667 --> 01:31:41,268
-You a friend of Chunk's?

1008
01:31:41,369 --> 01:31:44,638
-Gosh, no Ma'am, quite
the opposite if I am to confess.

1009
01:31:44,739 --> 01:31:48,042
I'm the sort generally plays
Coyote to Chunk's jackrabbit

1010
01:31:48,142 --> 01:31:49,510
if you take my meaning.

1011
01:31:49,610 --> 01:31:50,978
-You the law?

1012
01:31:51,078 --> 01:31:52,113
Not per se, Ma'am,

1013
01:31:52,279 --> 01:31:54,548
but I am registered official
with the State of Tennessee.

1014
01:31:54,648 --> 01:31:57,118
I am a bounty hunter by trade.

1015
01:31:57,218 --> 01:31:58,853
-Dandy thing like you?

1016
01:31:58,953 --> 01:32:02,189
-Truth be told, I'm just
passing through en route

1017
01:32:02,289 --> 01:32:03,557
to Fort McKinnley...

1018
01:32:03,657 --> 01:32:05,760
Managed to find myself
between watering holes

1019
01:32:05,860 --> 01:32:11,098
and wondered
if I might take the liberty.

1020
01:32:14,268 --> 01:32:16,170
Well's 'round back.

1021
01:32:16,670 --> 01:32:18,873
Much obliged.

1022
01:32:35,156 --> 01:32:36,857
-You hungry?

1023
01:32:42,129 --> 01:32:45,866
Some more of these Buckwheat
cakes for you, Mr. Lang?

1024
01:32:45,966 --> 01:32:50,971
-I couldn't possibly, Ma'am.
I'm about ready to burst.

1025
01:32:51,072 --> 01:32:54,742
-It's been a spell
since I cooked for a man.

1026
01:32:58,212 --> 01:33:01,048
-Must be hard
just the two of you out here.

1027
01:33:01,148 --> 01:33:03,350
How long's it been?

1028
01:33:03,451 --> 01:33:05,352
-Five years now.

1029
01:33:11,025 --> 01:33:14,361
-Must get mighty lonesome
sometimes.

1030
01:33:15,162 --> 01:33:19,233
-You sure you won't have
just one more, Mr. Lang?

1031
01:33:19,333 --> 01:33:21,168
-Maybe just one.

1032
01:33:29,777 --> 01:33:32,046
That is a nice laugh.

1033
01:33:37,418 --> 01:33:39,353
Good Heavens...

1034
01:33:40,589 --> 01:33:43,157
You have received the word.

1035
01:33:46,060 --> 01:33:47,828
-Yes, I have.

1036
01:33:50,631 --> 01:33:53,834
-He heals the broken-hearted...

1037
01:33:54,603 --> 01:33:57,671
He binds their wounds...

1038
01:33:57,771 --> 01:34:01,175
He's a father
to the fatherless...

1039
01:34:01,275 --> 01:34:08,816
A defender to widows is God
in his holy dwelling.

1040
01:34:13,187 --> 01:34:15,856
These last five years
must have been a chore

1041
01:34:15,956 --> 01:34:18,159
for you and the boy.

1042
01:34:23,297 --> 01:34:28,335
-Chunk was no prize
by any means, but...

1043
01:34:28,435 --> 01:34:31,005
I do miss him sometimes.

1044
01:34:33,741 --> 01:34:36,710
Miss havin' a man
around the house.

1045
01:34:41,882 --> 01:34:45,753
-When's the last time
someone's taken you to town...

1046
01:34:45,853 --> 01:34:49,089
Bought you a pretty dress
or the like?

1047
01:34:55,196 --> 01:34:59,400
-No one's taken me to town
in a long time.

1048
01:35:06,373 --> 01:35:08,008
Samuel.

1049
01:35:08,809 --> 01:35:11,245
Take Albert outside to play.

1050
01:35:11,345 --> 01:35:12,079
- <i>Okay, Mama.</i>

1051
01:35:12,179 --> 01:35:15,316
-And don't come back
until I call.

1052
01:35:36,737 --> 01:35:39,106
-What'd the old man want, Kate?

1053
01:35:42,376 --> 01:35:44,111
-Who?

1054
01:35:44,812 --> 01:35:48,683
-The old man that came by
two days ago.

1055
01:35:48,782 --> 01:35:53,588
Had a young boy
travelin' alongside him.

1056
01:35:53,688 --> 01:35:55,756
What'd he want?

1057
01:35:55,856 --> 01:35:57,525
-We ain't seen no one
like that--

1058
01:35:59,159 --> 01:36:03,764
-Samuel told me a boy and his
grandpa give him that pup

1059
01:36:03,864 --> 01:36:05,399
not just two days ago.

1060
01:36:05,499 --> 01:36:06,166
-He's imagining things.

1061
01:36:06,267 --> 01:36:11,272
-Oh, deliver my soul
from lying lips

1062
01:36:11,372 --> 01:36:14,643
and a deceitful tongue.

1063
01:36:14,743 --> 01:36:20,948
-He was here.
Two days ago, like you said.

1064
01:36:21,048 --> 01:36:24,985
I told him to leave
and that was the end of it.

1065
01:36:25,085 --> 01:36:27,589
-Which way did they go?

1066
01:36:27,689 --> 01:36:29,557
-South.

1067
01:36:29,658 --> 01:36:31,559
Down the valley.

1068
01:36:37,164 --> 01:36:41,101
You all horn
and no rattle, Mr. Lang?

1069
01:36:52,146 --> 01:36:53,847
-Ma'am.

1070
01:37:16,470 --> 01:37:18,439
- <i>Harland Rust!</i>

1071
01:37:23,578 --> 01:37:26,347
-Harland Rust, present yourself!

1072
01:37:28,015 --> 01:37:31,952
Got me a seasoned gunhand
out here, old man!

1073
01:37:33,487 --> 01:37:36,090
Do not be foolish!

1074
01:37:36,490 --> 01:37:40,160
You ain't chasin' the devil
'round this stump!

1075
01:37:41,161 --> 01:37:42,797
Show yourself I says!

1076
01:37:48,636 --> 01:37:51,472
Christ!
God, I'm hit!

1077
01:37:57,010 --> 01:37:58,245
- <i>Lucas!</i>

1078
01:37:58,345 --> 01:38:00,247
-I'm here!

1079
01:38:00,481 --> 01:38:02,349
- <i>Run!</i>

1080
01:38:27,509 --> 01:38:29,243
Get the rifle!

1081
01:38:45,593 --> 01:38:47,529
-Rust!

1082
01:38:47,629 --> 01:38:50,998
You son of a whore!

1083
01:38:57,938 --> 01:38:59,607
- <i>Come on.</i>

1084
01:39:11,051 --> 01:39:13,454
-It's not so bad...

1085
01:39:13,888 --> 01:39:16,591
I just wanna rest here
for a minute...

1086
01:39:19,960 --> 01:39:22,229
-Are you okay?

1087
01:39:22,496 --> 01:39:24,198
-I'm all right...

1088
01:39:25,466 --> 01:39:27,334
I've had worse...

1089
01:39:29,537 --> 01:39:32,072
Don't fret none.

1090
01:39:33,575 --> 01:39:35,275
It's all right.

1091
01:39:36,878 --> 01:39:39,279
We're gonna be all right.

1092
01:40:02,904 --> 01:40:05,773
-You're bleeding pretty bad.

1093
01:40:06,741 --> 01:40:08,208
-I've been hurt worse.

1094
01:40:08,308 --> 01:40:10,745
-Yeah, but you're not...

1095
01:40:11,613 --> 01:40:13,413
-What?

1096
01:40:13,715 --> 01:40:16,149
I'm not young anymore?

1097
01:40:16,985 --> 01:40:19,854
-I didn't mean that.

1098
01:40:19,954 --> 01:40:21,021
-I may be long in the tooth,

1099
01:40:21,121 --> 01:40:23,290
but I haven't had my horns
sawed off yet.

1100
01:40:23,390 --> 01:40:25,593
-Yeah, but if we can't
stop the bleeding--

1101
01:40:25,693 --> 01:40:29,597
-Lucas. It'll be all right.

1102
01:40:31,298 --> 01:40:34,368
I just have to rest here
for a spell.

1103
01:40:41,308 --> 01:40:45,613
You don't resemble
your mama none.

1104
01:40:46,014 --> 01:40:47,682
-I know.

1105
01:40:49,316 --> 01:40:51,418
My father neither.

1106
01:40:51,519 --> 01:40:53,287
-It's Celia.

1107
01:40:53,621 --> 01:40:55,255
Your grandma.

1108
01:40:56,024 --> 01:40:58,292
I married her after the war.

1109
01:40:58,392 --> 01:41:03,363
I was 38, she was 19,
your ma come the following year.

1110
01:41:04,933 --> 01:41:08,068
All went a cropper in '65.

1111
01:41:08,870 --> 01:41:11,471
Our boy Henry was born,
the next day she was out there

1112
01:41:11,573 --> 01:41:16,678
sandbagging with the rest of us,
trying to save the farm.

1113
01:41:17,745 --> 01:41:19,547
-The flood?

1114
01:41:19,647 --> 01:41:22,149
-Took everything we had.

1115
01:41:24,686 --> 01:41:26,453
Took my boy.

1116
01:41:30,525 --> 01:41:33,962
Bank come for the land
soon after that.

1117
01:41:34,227 --> 01:41:37,364
Celia wasn't the same anymore.

1118
01:41:37,464 --> 01:41:40,668
One day, she walked
into the South Grand River

1119
01:41:40,768 --> 01:41:44,404
and never come up.

1120
01:41:45,740 --> 01:41:48,208
Sent your Ma to live
with Celia's kin,

1121
01:41:48,308 --> 01:41:51,879
I figured I'd just...

1122
01:41:51,980 --> 01:41:54,414
Cut picket and drift.

1123
01:41:59,186 --> 01:42:00,755
-Why me?

1124
01:42:00,855 --> 01:42:03,123
-How do you mean?

1125
01:42:03,958 --> 01:42:06,761
-Why me and not her?

1126
01:42:06,861 --> 01:42:08,963
-I don't know.

1127
01:42:09,697 --> 01:42:15,435
I was never much good to her
or anybody else, I guess.

1128
01:42:20,207 --> 01:42:23,276
-How many men have you killed?

1129
01:42:28,883 --> 01:42:30,752
-I don't remember.

1130
01:42:47,835 --> 01:42:49,336
-That you, Ike?

1131
01:42:49,436 --> 01:42:51,839
My guns are in their leather.

1132
01:42:56,878 --> 01:43:00,480
-You turn around and go back
the way you come, Preacher.

1133
01:43:02,984 --> 01:43:04,451
-The old man do that to you?

1134
01:43:04,552 --> 01:43:07,055
-He's a curly wolf
that son of a bitch.

1135
01:43:07,155 --> 01:43:09,524
Ain't togged out
in no sheep's wool neither.

1136
01:43:09,624 --> 01:43:13,393
-Don't suppose you might flush
out a quail on my account.

1137
01:43:13,493 --> 01:43:14,494
-I said git God damnit.

1138
01:43:14,595 --> 01:43:18,298
We ain't in no sod pawing mood--

1139
01:43:26,339 --> 01:43:28,275
-Which way?

1140
01:43:28,375 --> 01:43:30,410
-He's headed over Dawes Pass.

1141
01:43:30,511 --> 01:43:33,346
Got about a half day
jump on you.

1142
01:43:33,948 --> 01:43:35,783
-God bless.

1143
01:45:26,961 --> 01:45:29,030
-Don't come no closer!

1144
01:45:52,954 --> 01:45:54,421
-Aim co-BAH!!

1145
01:45:55,523 --> 01:45:59,927
Aim co-BAH!! Aim co-BAH!!

1146
01:46:00,027 --> 01:46:01,796
Aim co-BAH!!

1147
01:46:01,896 --> 01:46:03,764
Aim co-BAH!!

1148
01:46:05,800 --> 01:46:07,434
-Trade...

1149
01:46:08,269 --> 01:46:10,705
This gun for the horse.

1150
01:46:11,672 --> 01:46:14,642
For the horse... Trade...

1151
01:46:20,982 --> 01:46:22,917
-Hay Stin ah-awn.

1152
01:46:23,217 --> 01:46:25,686
Hay Stin ah-awn!!

1153
01:46:57,285 --> 01:46:59,620
-Strange boy.

1154
01:47:36,257 --> 01:47:38,526
-Come on,
we're going in here!

1155
01:47:39,560 --> 01:47:43,197
-Now these sorrels
are Injun broke mind you.

1156
01:47:43,297 --> 01:47:44,265
I'm tellin' you,

1157
01:47:44,365 --> 01:47:45,833
you ain't never seen
a saddle tramp better on a horse

1158
01:47:45,933 --> 01:47:48,836
than these Cayuse
outta Oregon.

1159
01:47:48,936 --> 01:47:52,239
What they name them horses
for matter of fact.

1160
01:47:52,340 --> 01:47:54,775
Same as them Coo-e-tans...

1161
01:47:57,044 --> 01:48:00,414
Yeah, they's tryin' to make 'em
all into farmers now,

1162
01:48:00,514 --> 01:48:01,849
you believe that?

1163
01:48:01,949 --> 01:48:06,053
Ain't never seen an Injun raise
nothing but hell on a scalp.

1164
01:48:15,129 --> 01:48:20,067
Well, look what just blew in
with the tumbleweeds.

1165
01:48:25,473 --> 01:48:26,574
<i>I'm gonna go find some help.</i>

1166
01:48:26,674 --> 01:48:27,808
-I don't need any help.

1167
01:48:27,975 --> 01:48:29,710
-You're gonna die if I don't.
-They's payin' 25

1168
01:48:29,810 --> 01:48:30,945
for a Kiowa scalp now,

1169
01:48:31,045 --> 01:48:33,547
50 for the whole kit
and kaboodle.

1170
01:48:33,647 --> 01:48:36,350
And a Kaw'll get you 75 per.

1171
01:48:36,450 --> 01:48:38,986
-Is there a doctor nearabout?

1172
01:48:39,120 --> 01:48:41,789
-There was one with a line camp
pulling up stakes

1173
01:48:41,889 --> 01:48:43,591
about half a mile West
from here.

1174
01:48:43,691 --> 01:48:45,826
He might still be there.

1175
01:48:47,028 --> 01:48:49,864
-Stay here, I'll get back
as soon as I can.

1176
01:48:52,833 --> 01:48:55,770
-Yeah I was there in Nebraska
back in '79,

1177
01:48:55,870 --> 01:48:57,805
just outside Fort Robinson...

1178
01:48:57,905 --> 01:49:00,875
Them Northern Cheyenne
got loose...

1179
01:49:00,975 --> 01:49:03,210
Them Winchesters
set to rolling...

1180
01:49:04,612 --> 01:49:07,782
Kill't 75 of them
scalp lifters.

1181
01:49:36,177 --> 01:49:38,946
We came across three of them
Kiowa savages this morning

1182
01:49:39,046 --> 01:49:40,347
riding brush back
through that

1183
01:49:40,448 --> 01:49:42,450
cross canyon
six miles back.

1184
01:49:42,551 --> 01:49:46,521
One of 'em
had the prettiest Henry rifle

1185
01:49:46,620 --> 01:49:48,756
I ever put eyes on...

1186
01:49:48,856 --> 01:49:52,193
Nice alkaline gold filigree...

1187
01:49:58,666 --> 01:50:01,302
Stubborn mule just couldn't
let go of his Henry.

1188
01:50:08,109 --> 01:50:11,580
You know, supposedly there's
an old man and a boy

1189
01:50:11,679 --> 01:50:15,082
traveling South
through New Mexico...

1190
01:50:15,182 --> 01:50:18,520
They's offering a thousand
dollars on the both of them,

1191
01:50:18,619 --> 01:50:20,154
y'all hear that?

1192
01:50:20,254 --> 01:50:24,391
Then in these two blow
with the wind...

1193
01:50:30,064 --> 01:50:34,969
Hey, old friend, you look like
a corpse forgot to fall over.

1194
01:50:39,874 --> 01:50:42,877
Why don't you let
me buy you a drink?

1195
01:50:45,679 --> 01:50:47,648
Come on,
a little coffin varnish

1196
01:50:47,748 --> 01:50:50,818
ain't gonna put your soul
at risk none.

1197
01:50:53,020 --> 01:50:57,024
-Heaven ain't waitin'
on neither one of us.

1198
01:50:57,124 --> 01:50:58,959
-Amen to that.

1199
01:51:00,895 --> 01:51:05,232
How about you cool that saddle
for spell and stand up?

1200
01:51:08,335 --> 01:51:13,608
This thumb buster I got dangling
at my side ain't no watch charm.

1201
01:51:13,707 --> 01:51:16,877
I don't pack it for bluff
nor ballast.

1202
01:51:18,245 --> 01:51:23,217
I'm a high line rider, old man.
I'm telling you to stand up.

1203
01:51:29,423 --> 01:51:31,192
-Harland Rust.

1204
01:51:37,666 --> 01:51:42,036
I want you to stand up
nice and slow

1205
01:51:42,136 --> 01:51:44,138
and toss any shootin' irons
you got.

1206
01:51:44,238 --> 01:51:47,174
-Whoa, whoa, whoa,
we was conversatin' here.

1207
01:51:47,274 --> 01:51:49,276
-Conversation's over.

1208
01:51:49,578 --> 01:51:52,213
-Who's that sayin' so?

1209
01:51:57,785 --> 01:51:59,521
-The law.

1210
01:51:59,621 --> 01:52:02,256
-Ain't no law around here.

1211
01:52:04,291 --> 01:52:08,429
Ain't no iteration he's walking
out of here with you.

1212
01:52:22,776 --> 01:52:24,613
-Damnit!... Damnit!

1213
01:52:27,214 --> 01:52:29,817
-He hoorawed you good,
didn't he?!

1214
01:52:29,917 --> 01:52:31,586
-Shut the fuck up!

1215
01:52:31,686 --> 01:52:32,953
Put your fuckin' teeth away!

1216
01:52:33,053 --> 01:52:34,888
-He's gonna die,
you gotta help him!

1217
01:52:34,989 --> 01:52:36,591
-We're all gonna die.

1218
01:52:38,727 --> 01:52:40,761
-That bounty's mine!

1219
01:54:07,915 --> 01:54:09,950
-Lucas!

1220
01:54:30,971 --> 01:54:33,107
-God damnit, Drum...

1221
01:54:33,207 --> 01:54:37,411
-Aw Christ that's a God damn
two dollar shirt.

1222
01:54:39,781 --> 01:54:41,915
-Go on.

1223
01:55:56,758 --> 01:55:57,759
- <i>Lucas...</i>

1224
01:55:57,859 --> 01:55:59,527
-No...

1225
01:56:03,030 --> 01:56:04,732
Come on...

1226
01:56:06,200 --> 01:56:08,302
Come on, get up...

1227
01:56:17,110 --> 01:56:19,547
<i>You down there, old man?</i>

1228
01:56:37,932 --> 01:56:40,735
I don't like
your chances much on foot...

1229
01:56:43,370 --> 01:56:46,674
I used to go hunting
with my Daddy...

1230
01:56:58,118 --> 01:56:59,353
-I want you to go now, boy.

1231
01:56:59,453 --> 01:57:00,889
And don't stop for nothing.

1232
01:57:00,989 --> 01:57:02,824
I'm gonna hold him here
as best I can.

1233
01:57:02,924 --> 01:57:04,526
-I'm not leaving you...

1234
01:57:10,197 --> 01:57:12,534
-You gotta go...
-No!

1235
01:57:13,367 --> 01:57:15,202
-Come on!

1236
01:57:16,069 --> 01:57:18,305
- <i>Son of a bitch!</i>

1237
01:57:18,873 --> 01:57:20,575
<i>God damnit!</i>

1238
01:57:20,675 --> 01:57:22,342
<i>Fuck!</i>

1239
01:57:24,211 --> 01:57:26,848
-Stay here and look after Drum!

1240
01:57:27,015 --> 01:57:30,484
-God damnit you're not going
after him alone!

1241
01:57:45,800 --> 01:57:48,201
-Skin yourself of that weapon...

1242
01:57:48,302 --> 01:57:51,806
Or I'll put a hole
in the boy's head.

1243
01:57:52,472 --> 01:57:56,243
I ain't one to make
idle threats, Mr. Rust.

1244
01:58:11,593 --> 01:58:13,695
Formidable my ass.

1245
01:58:15,630 --> 01:58:19,399
- <i>No! No!</i>

1246
01:58:25,573 --> 01:58:27,842
-You let go of that boy
right now.

1247
01:58:27,942 --> 01:58:29,276
-Whoa now, Marshal...

1248
01:58:29,376 --> 01:58:32,212
Just take it easy,
slow down now...

1249
01:58:32,747 --> 01:58:35,650
I'm on this bounty
all legal and proper,

1250
01:58:35,750 --> 01:58:36,584
we's on the same side

1251
01:58:36,684 --> 01:58:39,486
now don't be a sore loser,
I got here first.

1252
01:58:39,587 --> 01:58:42,624
-Turn him loose,
we'll sort it out.

1253
01:58:42,724 --> 01:58:43,390
- <i>Can't do that.</i>

1254
01:58:43,490 --> 01:58:46,493
<i>Now you put that</i>
head cutter down.

1255
01:58:46,728 --> 01:58:50,263
-I'm giving you a lawful order,
turn him loose.

1256
01:58:50,364 --> 01:58:52,499
-Put it down...

1257
01:58:52,767 --> 01:58:54,869
Down, down, down, down...

1258
01:59:02,744 --> 01:59:04,545
There you go.

1259
01:59:05,780 --> 01:59:07,280
-Got more men coming.

1260
01:59:07,381 --> 01:59:10,551
Ain't no way out
but the way I come.

1261
01:59:10,785 --> 01:59:14,088
-God will show me the way.

1262
01:59:14,187 --> 01:59:16,124
For I am his servant...

1263
01:59:16,223 --> 01:59:19,827
I am God's angel of wrath
to bring punishment

1264
01:59:19,927 --> 01:59:22,030
upon the evil doer...

1265
01:59:22,130 --> 01:59:24,464
And this boy has sinned.

1266
01:59:25,432 --> 01:59:27,635
And he must pay the price.

1267
01:59:30,470 --> 01:59:32,840
Now let me do God's work.

1268
01:59:50,424 --> 01:59:54,529
Oh, shit.

1269
02:00:45,012 --> 02:00:46,614
-Grandpa!

1270
02:00:48,315 --> 02:00:49,117
- <i>No, don't touch it...</i>

1271
02:00:49,316 --> 02:00:51,485
<i>- </i> Just keep pressing on it!

1272
02:00:56,524 --> 02:00:58,626
-Where's Harland Rust?

1273
02:01:11,172 --> 02:01:14,575
God damnit...

1274
02:01:16,276 --> 02:01:18,012
How bad you hurt?

1275
02:01:24,384 --> 02:01:27,955
-You're that Marshal Helm
out of Wyoming.

1276
02:01:28,455 --> 02:01:31,259
-Nearly crossed paths
once or twice.

1277
02:01:31,358 --> 02:01:33,561
Twelve years ago in Missouri...

1278
02:01:33,728 --> 02:01:37,198
then again in Sheridan County,
'72.

1279
02:01:37,297 --> 02:01:39,667
-The Federal Bank in Kingman.

1280
02:01:39,767 --> 02:01:42,069
-That's right.

1281
02:01:42,170 --> 02:01:44,337
-Make a deal with you Marshal...

1282
02:01:44,437 --> 02:01:48,609
Let him go...
And I'll come quiet.

1283
02:01:49,243 --> 02:01:50,443
-I can't do that.

1284
02:01:50,545 --> 02:01:51,779
- <i>He's not a killer.</i>

1285
02:01:51,879 --> 02:01:53,614
-That ain't up to me.

1286
02:01:53,781 --> 02:01:55,883
-Thirteen year-old boy
goes back there to hang

1287
02:01:55,983 --> 02:01:57,785
for something that never
should have happened

1288
02:01:57,885 --> 02:01:59,419
in the first place?

1289
02:01:59,520 --> 02:02:00,688
Now where's the good in that?!

1290
02:02:00,788 --> 02:02:03,758
-It ain't my job
to decide that.

1291
02:02:05,893 --> 02:02:07,962
-You got a son, Marshal?

1292
02:02:09,697 --> 02:02:12,667
You let the boy
ride outta here...

1293
02:02:12,834 --> 02:02:17,305
And all the bad that come
from what he done ends here.

1294
02:02:17,404 --> 02:02:19,006
Or...

1295
02:02:19,106 --> 02:02:23,376
You'll be the first man
I truly regret killing.

1296
02:02:27,114 --> 02:02:28,816
You gotta go now, Lucas.

1297
02:02:28,916 --> 02:02:29,851
-Don't say that.

1298
02:02:30,585 --> 02:02:33,386
-Them other lawmen are gonna
be ridin' up from Mosquero.

1299
02:02:33,486 --> 02:02:34,487
I want you to ride South

1300
02:02:34,589 --> 02:02:35,923
-a day to Masilla...
-I can't...

1301
02:02:36,023 --> 02:02:39,961
You're gonna be looking
for a man named Anselmo...

1302
02:02:40,061 --> 02:02:42,230
My sister she--

1303
02:02:42,530 --> 02:02:44,599
Everything's been arranged.

1304
02:02:44,699 --> 02:02:46,200
He's gonna take you to Mexico.

1305
02:02:46,300 --> 02:02:47,535
-I can't do this by myself...

1306
02:02:47,635 --> 02:02:50,671
-Yes, you can...
yes, you can.

1307
02:02:52,640 --> 02:02:55,710
Now don't you cry
no tears for me...

1308
02:02:56,844 --> 02:02:57,845
You understand?

1309
02:02:57,945 --> 02:02:59,947
Never.

1310
02:03:01,381 --> 02:03:03,651
A man chooses who he is.

1311
02:03:11,225 --> 02:03:13,527
Don't you ever forget that.

1312
02:03:16,030 --> 02:03:17,765
-Lucas.

1313
02:03:18,431 --> 02:03:20,735
Lucas. Go on.

1314
02:03:26,841 --> 02:03:28,509
Go on.

1315
02:04:45,853 --> 02:04:47,788
-Elwood.

1316
02:04:47,888 --> 02:04:48,990
-Laurence.

1317
02:04:49,090 --> 02:04:50,458
-You all right?

1318
02:04:50,558 --> 02:04:51,491
-Yeah.

1319
02:04:51,659 --> 02:04:56,063
-Christ almighty.
So this is Harland Rust.

1320
02:04:58,366 --> 02:05:00,167
Where's the boy?

1321
02:05:01,469 --> 02:05:04,405
I asked you where's the boy,
God damnit?

1322
02:05:04,504 --> 02:05:06,307
-He made a run for it.

1323
02:05:06,407 --> 02:05:08,042
Him and his horse went
into the ravine,

1324
02:05:08,142 --> 02:05:09,377
fell a hundred foot.

1325
02:05:09,944 --> 02:05:13,748
Kiowa scavengers come for him
before we could get to the body.

1326
02:05:14,782 --> 02:05:17,218
-So I guess that's it then.

1327
02:05:18,652 --> 02:05:20,521
-I reckon.

1328
02:05:21,022 --> 02:05:23,524
-Get this son of a bitch
stitched up.

1329
02:05:23,624 --> 02:05:27,294
Ain't no point taking a dead man
back to hang.

1330
02:06:31,225 --> 02:06:33,194
-You the Hollister boy?

1331
02:06:33,828 --> 02:06:35,496
Harland's grandson?

1332
02:06:35,596 --> 02:06:37,231
-Yes, sir.

1333
02:06:38,567 --> 02:06:40,768
-The old man about?

1334
02:06:41,635 --> 02:06:43,737
-It's just me now.

1335
02:06:45,940 --> 02:06:47,542
-Okay.

1336
02:06:47,842 --> 02:06:49,944
Name's Anselmo.

1337
02:06:51,412 --> 02:06:53,347
-I'm Lucas.

1338
02:06:54,081 --> 02:06:55,616
Lucas Rust.

1339
02:07:02,089 --> 02:07:04,593
-Sure you don't wanna come with?

1340
02:07:04,692 --> 02:07:07,128
-Think I'll ride home alone.

1341
02:07:07,394 --> 02:07:09,630
-All right then, Wood.

1342
02:07:10,599 --> 02:07:12,333
Hell of a job.

1343
02:07:13,267 --> 02:07:15,336
See you back in Sedgwick.

1344
02:07:34,523 --> 02:07:36,690
<i>- Hiya!</i>

1345
02:08:49,797 --> 02:08:52,233
- <i>It's time, Harland.</i>

1346
02:08:52,333 --> 02:08:54,468
<i>Get him up.</i>

1347
02:09:12,687 --> 02:09:14,255
-Got a stiff rope
and a short drop

1348
02:09:14,355 --> 02:09:16,223
waitin' on you, old man.

1349
02:09:51,091 --> 02:09:53,728
-Go forth Christian soul
from this world

1350
02:09:53,827 --> 02:09:56,897
in the name of God
the almighty...

1351
02:09:56,997 --> 02:09:59,133
We pray Heavenly Father,
this day,

1352
02:09:59,233 --> 02:10:03,738
for your divine justice,
grace and mercy.

1353
02:10:03,837 --> 02:10:05,239
Amen.

1354
02:10:05,339 --> 02:10:06,974
-Um...uh...

1355
02:10:07,074 --> 02:10:09,544
I think this man's dead,
Marshal.

1356
02:10:12,514 --> 02:10:14,982
-Kill him twice then.

1357
02:10:43,477 --> 02:10:45,212
-Lucas!

1358
02:19:11,052 --> 02:19:12,687
<i>- Coming back</i>
<i> to be part of the completion</i>

1359
02:19:12,787 --> 02:19:14,121
<i>of the filming of Rust</i>
<i> after the tragedy</i>

1360
02:19:14,222 --> 02:19:17,158
<i>that took Halyna's life</i>
<i>was the most difficult decision</i>

1361
02:19:17,258 --> 02:19:18,491
<i>I've ever had to make.</i>

1362
02:19:18,593 --> 02:19:20,493
<i>But I knew that it was</i>
<i> the wish of Halyna's family</i>

1363
02:19:20,595 --> 02:19:22,495
<i>that her final word</i>
<i> not simply vanish,</i>

1364
02:19:22,597 --> 02:19:23,798
<i>that it could be seen</i>
<i>and appreciated,</i>

1365
02:19:23,898 --> 02:19:26,200
<i>that people would have</i>
<i> the opportunity to discover</i>

1366
02:19:26,300 --> 02:19:28,401
<i>how uniquely talented she was,</i>

1367
02:19:28,501 --> 02:19:30,470
<i>that they could see the world</i>
<i> through her eyes,</i>

1368
02:19:30,571 --> 02:19:33,140
<i>even if just for a few hours.</i>

1369
02:19:33,241 --> 02:19:34,175
<i>For the crew that returned</i>

1370
02:19:34,342 --> 02:19:35,408
<i>and the new crew members</i>
<i>that joined us,</i>

1371
02:19:35,509 --> 02:19:38,411
<i>we completed Rust</i>
<i> to celebrate our friend Halyna</i>

1372
02:19:38,512 --> 02:19:39,614
<i>her art, her talent,</i>

1373
02:19:39,714 --> 02:19:44,018
<i>and the indelible legacy</i>
<i>she left behind.</i>